course: dictionary
lesson: 14772
title: Things that stick out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To protrude means to stick out from a surface or edge. Think of a pencil poking out of the top of a pencil case: it is sticking out past the edge.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «A nail was protruding from the wooden fence.» A nail that sticks out of wood can catch on your clothes, so protruding must mean sticking out.
explain: Protrude is a verb, so its form changes: protrudes, protruded, protruding. «The frog's eyes protrude from its head.» The picture of eyes sticking out helps you remember the word.
fact: Protrude means to stick out from a surface or edge.
fact: «Protruding» is the form of protrude used with «is» or «was», as in «a nail was protruding».
fact: «Protruded» is the past form: «A small root protruded from the soil.»
fact: In science, animals such as frogs can have protruding eyes, which means their eyes stick out from their head.
fact: A good check is to swap in «stick out» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «A nail was protruding from the wooden fence.» What does protruding mean? | *Sticking out from a surface | Lying flat on the ground | Shining brightly | Sinking into the water
exercise: «Her front teeth protruded a little when she smiled.» Which word tells you the teeth stuck out? | little | front | smiled | *protruded
exercise: Why can a protruding nail be dangerous? | Because it turns into a flower | Because it makes the wood lighter | *Because it can catch on clothes and scratch you | Because it makes the fence smell nice
test: «A small root protruded from the soil.» What does protruded mean? | Was painted | Sank down | Melted | *Stuck out
test: Ella says protrude means to hide inside something. What is the right meaning? | Fall off a table | To hide inside something | Make a loud noise | *To stick out from a surface or edge
exam: «Tom's shirt tag protrudes from his collar, so he tucks it in.» What does protrudes mean here? | It is wet | *It sticks out | It is new | It is hidden
